# Clearpay Customer Mobile — API

## Base URL and versioning

- API base URL comes from environment configuration
  (`EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL`), never hard-coded per screen.
- Call versioned customer routes under `/api/v1/customer/` (see Clearpay backend
  docs: `API.md`, `API_CUSTOMER.md`, `API_CUSTOMER_AUTH.md`).
- Do not invent endpoints, query keys, or body fields.

## Response format

Expect the Clearpay JSON envelope:

- Success: `{ success: true, data, message, meta }`
- Error: `{ success: false, error: { code, message, details? } }`
- Paginated lists: items in `data` (or `data.items` per resource docs) with
  `meta: { page, limit, total, totalPages }`

Normalize errors into a single client error type for UI and Query `onError`
handlers. Do not parse ad-hoc shapes per screen.

## Auth headers

- Send `Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>` on protected routes.
- Access / refresh tokens live in SecureStore.
- On refresh failure or unrecoverable `401`, clear the session and route to
  sign-in.
- Never attach tokens to non-API requests or third-party URLs.

## Pagination

Use the backend pagination contract (`page`, `limit`, `sort`, `order`) and map
it through TanStack Query infinite/list queries. Do not invent client-side
paging over full dumps.

## Authority

- No direct database access from the mobile app.
- No client-side authority over financial data (balances, refunds, captures,
  ledger correctness). Display what the API returns; mutations go through
  documented REST endpoints only.
- Money is integer minor units (`amountMinor`). Never use floats for money.
- Public IDs only (`cus_…`, `pay_…`, `txn_…`) — never Mongo ObjectIds as client
  identifiers.
